           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0001-3704-3149")))
Description: Adverse-event tables in trial registries and journals often list an
    event only if it exceeds a frequency threshold in at least one arm. Among the
    rows that are listed, the arm that crosses the threshold more easily has its
    event rate pushed up more, which biases pooled drug-placebo risk ratios.
    The package gives the exact conditional moments of a posted row, the
    distortion expected for a set of trials, the posting rules, Mantel-Haenszel
    and inverse-variance pooling, and a selection-corrected random-effects
    likelihood for a common risk ratio.
